Hello hello hello! Here are the latest patch notes for the premiere build of Sigh of the Abyss:
Voice acting
•	Restored missing voice acting to the very first scenes with Malec and Atri;
•	Added voice acting to two more chapters of the game (the dance party, endings and epilogues are still a work in progress);
•	Minor fixes to Alpheon's first introduction (restored a missing voice line);
Text issues
•	Added some clarification to the diplomatic path with Valerico;
•	Fixed a codex tooltip when going to LaMarina;
•	Added some clarification to a conversation with Ascanio regarding the Halls' magick;
•	Added a line to make a scene with Sylas less abrupt if you're on friendly terms with Renza;
•	Changed the name of Sylas' first date event to be clearer;
•	A couple more assorted text fixes;
Other
•	Fixed the scene transition when returning to LaMarina;
•	Fixed character positions when returning from the docks;
•	Fixed the Envoy's cape sudden disappearance in Bástian's scene;
•	Made the background music in Alpheon's introduction smoother;
•	Made the background music in Enilia's introduction smoother;
•	Unlocking the romance preferences will now bring up the stat menu, so you can customize them right away!
•	After being jump scared by the bell one too many times, finally lowered its volume;
•	Atri respects your personal space now in your scene with her, after you have access to The Refrain;
•	Made the transition to the Halls' video background smoother;
•	Lowered the volume of the Halls' waterfall;
•	Fixed the Envoy's position when talking to the siren;

Known issues
•	Auto-saves misbehave. It looks like you only have one, and the rest of the page is empty. Temporary fix: go to the second page of auto-saves and return to the first. The auto-saves will be there again;

If you  encounter any bugs during your playthrough, send them my way!

I'll push another patch very soon with the rest of the voice acting and more fixes.
